# Event Delegation (Load More / AJAX Grid Safety)

Mandatory for every grid and card interaction: shop archives, product
collections, filters, Load More, and anything else that appends DOM nodes after
page load.

The failure this prevents is expensive to find, because it does not reproduce on
the first page. A handler bound directly to `.sk-swatch` elements at
`DOMContentLoaded` works perfectly until Load More appends page 2, at which
point the new cards are inert with no error in the console.

## Shared module

`src/js/shared/delegated-events.js`

| Export | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `delegateDocument( eventType, selector, handler )` | Bind once on `document`; handler receives `( event, matchedElement )` |
| `delegateOn( root, eventType, selector, handler )` | Same, scoped to a stable ancestor when `document` is too broad |
| `dispatchContentUpdated( detail )` | Fire `skaflow:content-updated` on `document` after AJAX appends nodes |
| `CONTENT_UPDATED_EVENT` | The event name constant |
| `isQueryRoot( node )` | Runtime check for a `querySelectorAll` root. Never `instanceof ParentNode` — that mixin is not a JS constructor and throws. |

Import from `src/js/index.js` or from a block's `view.js`. Existing consumers to
copy from: `shared/load-more.js`, `shared/product-grid-swatches.js`,
`shared/product-card-add-to-cart.js`, `shared/wishlist.js`, `product-filters.js` (modules in `product-filters/`),
`quick-view.js`.

## Rule 1 — delegate repeatable interactions

Click, hover, and keyboard handlers for cards, swatches, and pagination controls
must never call `addEventListener` directly on an element inside a grid.

```js
// ✅ Load-More-safe
import { delegateDocument } from './shared/delegated-events';

delegateDocument( 'click', '.sk-swatch', ( event, swatch ) => {
	// ...
} );

// ❌ Breaks silently on page 2+
document.querySelectorAll( '.sk-swatch' ).forEach( ( el ) => {
	el.addEventListener( 'click', handler );
} );
```

In JSX blocks, prefer React synthetic events on components you own, and delegate
at a parent level when mixing with server-rendered WooCommerce markup.

## Rule 2 — idempotent lazy init for real per-element setup

Features needing one-time library init (Swiper, `wc_variation_form()`) cannot be
delegated. They must instead:

1. Guard with a flag — `.sk-initialized` or `data-sk-initialized`.
2. Re-scan on `skaflow:content-updated` after AJAX, rather than re-binding
   interaction handlers.

```js
import {
	CONTENT_UPDATED_EVENT,
	dispatchContentUpdated,
} from './shared/delegated-events';

document.addEventListener( CONTENT_UPDATED_EVENT, initCarousels );

function initCarousels() {
	document
		.querySelectorAll( '.sk-carousel:not(.sk-initialized)' )
		.forEach( ( el ) => {
			el.classList.add( 'sk-initialized' );
			// new Swiper( el, ... )
		} );
}

// After a Load More append:
dispatchContentUpdated( { source: 'load-more' } );
```

Purely delegated handlers — grid swatch image swap, limit-swatches expand — do
**not** need `skaflow:content-updated`. Delegation already covers new nodes.

